 skew-y))\; transform-origin: var(--origin-x) var(--origin-y)\; } Join us f
 or an inspiring afternoon at the Petaluma Arts Center for Teaching As Art 
 Practice \, a panel discussion exploring the dynamic relationship between 
 teaching and creative practice. Drawing from Aristotle’s quote\, “Thos
 e who can\, do\; those who understand\, teach\,” this conversation bring
 s together artist educators from across the North Bay to discuss how teach
 ing art shapes\, challenges\, and enriches their own artistic work. Throug
 h personal experiences and shared perspectives\, panelists will reflect on
  mentorship\, creative process\, pedagogy\, and the evolving role of educa
 tors within contemporary art communities. The panel features professors an
 d teachers from Sonoma State University\, College of Marin\, and Santa Ros
 a Junior College. Moderated by New Voices Curator Emma Logan \, this engag
 ing discussion offers insight into the intersection of artmaking\, educati
 on\, and community connection. #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1781805721920_3884 { } 
